Keep a directory listing whole while its entries are being deleted.

ntfs3 hands out readdir positions that are byte offsets inside an index
block. Deleting an entry moves the ones after it down, so a position handed
out before the deletion points past entries nobody has seen, and they are
skipped. Finder deletes as it lists, and ends with "some items had to be
skipped". Positions now carry the directory's deletion count, and a stale
one starts the listing again after the dots.

